      "trialState": "evidence",
      "question": "Does the court admit E-01, Examiner’s report, over Mr. Ashby's challenge?",
      "context": "Mr. Ashby challenges E-01 (introduced): “Your Honour, the prosecution accepts the examiner's report on time and mechanism. It does not accept the last finding as it has been put. The examiner records five marks on a forearm and calls them a hand. Four outside, one inside is the shape of any grasp on a thin arm, whatever grasped it. The officer says neither unit's gripping surface matches the manufacturer's record. A record is a drawing. A frail man's arm, held hard for a moment, is not. Before the court takes it that a human hand held Edmund Halloway, I ask that the attribution be marked as opinion, not finding, and that the examiner's basis for excluding the units be put on the record. The bruise says he was held. It does not yet say by whom.” The exhibit: County examiner’s report. Time of death 22:55, plus or minus three minutes. Fatal injury to the back of the skull consistent with a fall down the full flight of the main staircase. Fresh bruising on the right forearm, four marks on the outer side and one on the inner, formed in the minutes before death. No other injuries. Blood alcohol nil.",
