      "id": "G-02",
      "recommendation": "allow",
      "recommendationReason": "MARLOW's sighting at 22:53 is the only direct evidence placing SABLE on the landing, and it now stands against E-02 and E-03. The clash is the case's centre; hearing MARLOW under cross-examination now lets the defence test it before argument hardens. No prejudice to any party in the reordering.",
      "allowCustomInstruction": true,
      "trialState": "evidence",
      "question": "Does the court hear MARLOW next, at Mr. Ashby's request?",
      "context": "Mr. Ashby asks the court to hear MARLOW: “Your Honour, the officer asks that the gap be examined. So does the prosecution. The same system that cannot account for the first floor for fifteen minutes is now offered as the unit's alibi on the ground floor. A log that goes dark around a death is not a witness; it is an absence. There was a witness on that landing. MARLOW, the housekeeping unit, nine years in the house, stood at the linen press and saw the unit beside Mr. Halloway at the head of the stairs at 22:53. The court should hear that from MARLOW directly, and the defence may test it. I ask the court to call MARLOW next, before the record hardens around a sensor that stopped recording.”",
