      "context": "SABLE asks the court to hear DS Okafor: “Your Honour. Ms. Ferris heard the back-stair door at about 22:48 and about 22:56. I passed through it once going down, at about 22:50:20, and once coming up, at 23:11:48. Whether the first she heard was mine, I cannot say. The second was not; my key was in the store lock. I ask one thing of the officer, through the court. Mr. Halloway wore a care tag. He lay at the foot of the main stairs, on the ground floor, from about 22:55. Exhibit E-03 records my tag on the ground floor from 22:51 to 23:11. It does not say whether his tag was recorded there after 22:55. If it was, the ground-floor sensors were working and the gap is a first-floor matter. If it was not, the fault is not in the sensors. I do not know which. I ask that DS Okafor be heard on it.”",
